examples.question_text:
The graph shows $y=f(x)$ with an orange tangent at $P$, where $x=3$. Estimate $f'(3)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{tangentOrange}{HTML}{EF8B2C}
\definecolor{gridGrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridGrey,very thin] (0,0) grid (6,5);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(6.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5,6} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.1) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\v in {1/2,2/4,3/6,4/8,5/10} {\draw[black] (0,\y)--(-0.1,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[curveBlue,thick,domain=0:6,samples=81,variable=\x] plot (\x,{0.1*(\x-3)*(\x-3)+0.5*\x+1});
\draw[tangentOrange,thick] (0,1)--(6,4);
\fill[black] (3,2.5) circle (2pt) node[above left] {$P$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Read two points on the tangent: $(0,2)$ and $(6,8)$. The vertical scale is $2$ units per grid square.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{tangentOrange}{HTML}{EF8B2C}
\draw[tangentOrange,thick] (0,0)--(4,2);
\draw[black,dashed] (0,0)--(4,0) node[midway,below] {run $=6$};
\draw[black,dashed] (4,0)--(4,2) node[midway,right] {rise $=6$};
\fill[black] (0,0) circle (2pt) node[above left] {$(0,2)$};
\fill[black] (4,2) circle (2pt) node[above left] {$(6,8)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The instantaneous rate of change is the tangent's gradient.

$\begin{aligned} f'(3)&\approx\dfrac{8-2}{6-0}\\&=\dfrac{6}{6}\\&=1 \end{aligned}$

examples.question_text:
The graph shows the temperature $T$ of a cooling object after $t$ minutes. The orange tangent is drawn at $t=8$. Estimate the instantaneous rate of change of temperature at this time.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{tangentOrange}{HTML}{EF8B2C}
\definecolor{gridGrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridGrey,very thin] (0,0) grid (6,5);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(6.5,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,5.5) node[above] {$T$};
\foreach \x/\v in {1/4,2/8,3/12,4/16,5/20,6/24} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.1) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\foreach \y/\v in {1/10,2/20,3/30,4/40,5/50} {\draw[black] (0,\y)--(-0.1,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\node[below] at (3,-0.65) {Time (min)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-0.95,2.5) {Temperature ($^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$)};
\draw[curveBlue,thick,domain=0:6,samples=81,variable=\x] plot (\x,{3*exp(-(\x-2)/3)});
\draw[tangentOrange,thick] (0,5)--(5,0);
\fill[black] (2,3) circle (2pt) node[above right] {$P$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Read the tangent's intercepts $(0,50)$ and $(20,0)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{tangentOrange}{HTML}{EF8B2C}
\draw[tangentOrange,thick] (0,2.5)--(4,0);
\draw[black,dashed] (0,2.5)--(4,2.5) node[midway,above] {run $=20$ min};
\draw[black,dashed] (4,2.5)--(4,0) node[midway,right] {change $=-50^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$};
\fill[black] (0,2.5) circle (2pt) node[left] {$(0,50)$};
\fill[black] (4,0) circle (2pt) node[below] {$(20,0)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\begin{aligned} T'(8)&\approx\dfrac{0-50}{20-0}\\&=\dfrac{-50}{20}\\&=-2.5\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C/min} \end{aligned}$

The temperature is decreasing by approximately $2.5^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ per minute at $t=8$ minutes.
